        },
        "text": "thinking about that time like a week ago when @alexandr_wang announced some sort of vague history project with Zach Bryan??"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-06-09T22:22:25.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1799930074772500687"
        ],
        "id": "1799930074772500687",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 11,
          "impression_count": 20617,
          "like_count": 62,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 6
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1799930073241592109",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "6/ so we won't see what would happen if you spent $100B of GPUs on a model for a while because of how spread out the GPU distributions are.\n\nwe'd likely need to see $500B of aggregate GPU spend to have an individual model trained on $100B of GPUs (wow!)"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-06-09T22:22:25.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1799930073241592109"
        ],
        "id": "1799930073241592109",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 40,
          "impression_count": 15896,
          "like_count": 94,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 6
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1799930071114760230",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "5/ there is another factor—which is that the $100B is spread between multiple labs.\n\nthe largest labs (Google, OpenAI, Meta, Anthropic, etc.) may only have 10-20% of the total GPU supply from NVDA\n\n(sidenote: Google is the hardest to track because they use TPUs as well as GPUs) https://t.co/hfcoO8TauE"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-06-09T22:22:24.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1799930071114760230"
        ],
        "id": "1799930071114760230",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 4,
          "impression_count": 13119,
          "like_count": 55,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 3
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1799930068661145818",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "7/ in the \"data wall will slow AI\" case, progress will depend on:\n\n- methods for data abundance (above)\n- algorithmic advances that advance us beyond the current scaling law paradigm"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-06-09T22:22:24.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1799930068661145818"
        ],
        "id": "1799930068661145818",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 10,
          "impression_count": 14372,
          "like_count": 72,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 3,
          "retweet_count": 3
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1799930066518098081",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "6/ if you zoomed all the way out, the data wall will either look like:\n\nA) a short-term impediment that we will engineer our way out of\nB) a very meaningful plateau to AI progress\n\nthe industry is pretty split on which of these it is—there's no obvious answer"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-06-09T22:22:23.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1799930066518098081"
        ],
        "id": "1799930066518098081",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 33,
          "impression_count": 30936,
          "like_count": 106,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 6,
          "retweet_count": 7
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1799930064957776091",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "4/ there's a lot of arguments on both ends, but fundamentally scaling relies on expanding beyond existing internet data\n\nwe need a number of methods for data abundance:\n- high-end expert frontier data, which is more valuable than internet data\n- RL environments\n- synthetic data"
      }
